<title>UK: European cotton markets see active price-testing.</title>
<headline>European cotton markets see active price-testing.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, England 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>European cotton markets attracted little firm business, despite active price-testing enquiry, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>Spinners remained reluctant to accept higher quotations given trade concern over the quality of current Northern Hemisphere crops.</p>
<p>Most prices were quoted unchanged.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +0171 542 8071</p>
